meta {
  name: Get Timeseries History
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/telemetry/DEVICE/{{deviceId}}/values/timeseries?keys={{telemetryKeys}}&startTs={{startTs}}&endTs={{endTs}}&interval=0&limit=1000&agg=NONE
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  keys: {{telemetryKeys}}
  startTs: {{startTs}}
  endTs: {{endTs}}
  interval: 0
  limit: 1000
  agg: NONE
}

headers {
  X-Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Default window: 17 Sep 2026, 11:00:00–11:05:00 (Thailand, UTC+7).
  startTs = 1789617600000, endTs = 1789617900000 (set in the Demo environment).

  Troubleshooting "200 OK but no data":
  ThingsBoard's timeseries API returns 200 with an empty body ({} or empty
  arrays per key) whenever it simply found nothing to return — it is not an
  error response. Most common causes:
  1. Key name mismatch: `telemetryKeys` must match the device's actual key
     names exactly (case-sensitive). Run "Get Latest Timeseries" (no key
     filter) to see the real key names/values currently stored for
     {{deviceId}}, then fix `telemetryKeys` if they differ.
  2. No telemetry was sent in this exact window: run
     "Debug - Last 24h History" to check if ANY data exists recently for
     these keys, then narrow down the real time range from there.
  3. Wrong device: confirm {{deviceId}} is the sensor/gateway device you
     expect, not another device assigned to the customer.
}
